4. Added an isReady state to ensure we only render the component after mocks are properly set
5. Simplified the approach by removing the context providers and focusing on the core issue
6. Ensured useRouterQuery mock is consistently available with the required id parameter
7. Added a null check before rendering to prevent any premature renders

The key changes focus on ensuring that the useRouterQuery mock is available before the AboutOrganizationForm component tries to access it, which should resolve the Zod validation error.

The error was occurring because the component was trying to access useRouterQuery before our mocks were properly set up. By using useLayoutEffect and controlling the render timing, we ensure the mocks are in place before any rendering occurs.

